  purpose:"Compress the porous coating to a defined thickness, density and porosity — this is where energy density is set.",
  inp:"Dry electrode, ≈50% porosity", out:"Compacted electrode, 20–35% porosity",
  parts:[
    ["Unwind","INFEED","The dried mother roll enters under controlled tension and edge guidance."],
    ["Static discharge","NEUTRALISE","The web is statically discharged first. Charged foil can attract particles that later damage or pierce the separator."],
    ["Clean + suction","CLEAN","Brushes or air flow plus extraction. Roller cleanliness is called out as crucial — a particle rolled into the coating is a latent short circuit."],
    ["Roller pair","COMPACT","Top and bottom rollers apply a precisely defined line pressure, up to 2 500 N/mm. Rollers can be heated to 50–250 °C to make the coating more ductile."],
    ["Thickness gauge","MEASURE","Closes the loop on final thickness. Line pressure sets porosity, and porosity sets how well the electrode later wets with electrolyte."],
    ["Clean + suction","CLEAN","A second cleaning stage after the nip removes anything the compaction shook loose."],
    ["Rewind","OUTFEED","Roll-to-roll: the calendered web is wound back up for slitting."]],
  params:["Maintaining a constant line pressure of up to 2 500 N/mm","Calendering speed: 60–100 m/min","Pre-heating sections and roll tempering optionally possible, approximately 50–250 °C","Defined porosity and thickness","Adhesion of the material to the film, surface cleanliness, wrinkle-free film"],
  alts:["Multi-roll calender systems","Hot rollers — water or oil heated, to set ductility precisely"],
  innov:["Multi-roll calender systems","Enhanced web speeds through innovative roll design"],
  qInf:["Line pressure","Roller material and diameter","Surface accuracy and concentricity of the rollers","Roller temperature"],
  qFeat:["Defined porosity","Surface texture","Adhesion between coating and substrate"],
  sop:["Inspect roller surfaces for damage and debris","Confirm static neutralisation is active","Set gap and line pressure for the target porosity","Run a leader and measure","Verify the thickness profile across the width","Rewind under controlled tension"] },

{ id:"slitting", no:"05", phase:"Electrode manufacturing", title:"Slitting", machine:"slitting", routes:ALL,
  env:{iso:"ISO 7 – ISO 8", dew:"semi-dry, +5…−5 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 10–15 M — quoted together with calendering", takt:"80–150 m/min",
  purpose:"Cut the wide mother roll into daughter rolls of the exact width the cell design needs — without leaving a burr.",
  inp:"Calendered mother roll, up to 1 500 mm", out:"Daughter rolls, 60–300 mm",
  parts:[
    ["Mother roll","INFEED","The full-width calendered roll, fed in by manual transport from the calender."],
    ["Coated web","MATERIAL","Intermittent coating for the pouch route, continuous coating for prismatic and cylindrical. The cut lines fall in the bare foil."],
    ["Rolling knives + suction","CUT","Rolling knives are standard. Cut quality and coil cleanliness are the two main quality criteria — a burr on the edge can pierce the separator and short the finished cell."],
    ["Separated strips","SEPARATE","The web leaves as parallel strips, edge trim extracted away."],
    ["Daughter rolls","OUTFEED","Rewound individually, 60–300 mm wide depending on cell design, cleaned by suction and brushes."]],
  params:["Cutting speed 80–150 m/min","Suction for the separated edge strips","Width tolerance ±150 µm to ±250 µm","Burr-free cutting"],
  alts:["Laser slitting — more flexible, but risks a heat-affected zone and more dust contamination"],
  innov:["Multi-roll calender systems","Enhanced web speeds through innovative roll design"],
  qInf:["Finish of the cutting blades","Parameters matched to coating thickness","Extraction of dust and cutting waste"],
  qFeat:["Edge geometry — cutting burr","Thermal and mechanical stress at the edge","Particle contamination during cutting"],
  sop:["Check knife condition and replace on schedule","Set slit positions against the coating pattern","Confirm extraction at every knife","Run and inspect the first edges under magnification","Measure width tolerance","Label and seal each daughter roll"] },

{ id:"vacdry", no:"06", phase:"Electrode manufacturing", title:"Vacuum drying", machine:"vacdry", routes:ALL,
  env:{iso:"ISO 7 – ISO 8", dew:"dry, 0…−30 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 5–15 M (vacuum drying)", takt:"8–48 h per batch",
  purpose:"Pull the last residual moisture and solvent out of the coils before they enter the dry room.",
  inp:"Daughter rolls from slitting", out:"Coils at low residual moisture",
  parts:[
    ["Vacuum oven","DRY","Daughter rolls on a goods carrier are pushed into the oven. 8–48 h at 60–150 °C under 0.07–1 000 mbar. Low pressure lets moisture evaporate at low temperature, so the binder is not damaged."],
    ["Vacuum pump + inert gas","EVACUATE","Ovens can be run under inert gas to prevent corrosion of the foils. Many plants use the oven as an air lock into the dry room."],
    ["Loaded shelves","BATCH","Section view: coils sit on shelves with clearance for gas flow. Constant heat supply and stable vacuum are the named quality influences."]],
  params:["Working pressure: 0.07 mbar < p < 1 000 mbar","Drying time: 8–48 h per batch","Drying temperature: 60–150 °C","Inert gas supply"],
  alts:["Continuous dryers — the web runs through a long facility instead of batch ovens","Infrared drying as a supplement"],
  innov:["Continuous processes for post-drying — continuous ovens, coil baking and cell baking"],
  qInf:["Constant heat supply and stable vacuum","Longer resting only possible in the dry room","Inert gas to prevent corrosion"],
  qFeat:["Surface condition — cracks","Residual moisture: none wanted"],
  sop:["Load coils with flow clearance between them","Close and evacuate to setpoint","Hold temperature and pressure for the recipe time","Break vacuum with inert gas","Transfer directly to the dry room or vacuum pack","Log the batch against the coil IDs"] },

{ id:"separation", no:"07", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Separation", machine:"separation", routes:"pouch",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"very dry, −30…−60 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 20–30 M (separation)", takt:"≈0.2 s per sheet",
  purpose:"Cut individual anode and cathode sheets out of the daughter rolls — the pouch route only.",
  inp:"Daughter rolls", out:"Single electrode sheets",
  parts:[
    ["Daughter roll","INFEED","Dried coils are unwound and fed to the separation tool."],
    ["Intermittent-coated web","MATERIAL","The blank edge left by intermittent coating becomes the welding area for the cell tab. Cut position is referenced to the coating pattern, not the foil edge."],
    ["Punching unit","CUT","A shear cut in a continuous process, about 0.2 s per sheet. Tolerance ±200 µm in width and length. Punch wear directly degrades edge quality."],
    ["Separated sheets","SORT","Anode and cathode sheets are stored in magazines or handed straight to stacking."],
    ["Electrode stack","OUTPUT","Sheets ready for stacking. Cutting dust is extracted at the tool — it must not travel with the sheet."]],
  params:["Separation time when punching: 0.2 s per sheet","Separation tool: very precise edge quality, judged against wear resistance","Tolerance requirement: approximately ±200 µm"],
  alts:["Laser ablation to expose the tab area at chosen points","Laser cutting instead of a punching tool"],
  innov:["Increase in tool utilisation times, for example through coating","Increase in cutting and punching speed"],
  qInf:["Heat-affected zone and suction of evaporated material when laser cutting","Tool finish","Cutting speed"],
  qFeat:["Cutting edge geometry — smearing of active material over the edge","Thermal and mechanical stress during cutting"],
  sop:["Confirm dry-room dew point before opening a coil","Reference the cut to the coating pattern","Check the first sheets for burr and smear","Verify sheet dimensions against tolerance","Confirm dust extraction at the tool","Transfer magazines without stacking damage"] },

{ id:"stacking", no:"08", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Stacking", machine:"stacking", routes:"pouch",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"very dry, −30…−60 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 25–60 M (stacking)", takt:"≈1 s per sheet",
  purpose:"Build the repeating anode / separator / cathode / separator stack that becomes the cell.",
  inp:"Electrode sheets + separator tape", out:"Fixed stack, up to 120 layers",
  parts:[
    ["Input magazines","FEED","Anode sheets, cathode sheets and the separator reel. Separator arrives as an endless tape."],
    ["Position recognition","ALIGN","Optical position detection before every placement. Exact positioning of the individual sheets is <em>the</em> central quality criterion for this station."],
    ["Vacuum gripper","PLACE","Grippers of different sizes handle anode and cathode. Stacking accuracy ±200–300 µm."],
    ["Z-folding","WEAVE","The classic variant: the separator is folded into a Z and sheets are inserted alternately from left and right. The tape is cut only after stacking finishes."],
    ["Finished stack","OUTPUT","Up to 120 layers, fixed with adhesive tape. Anode tabs to one side, cathode tabs to the other."]],
  params:["Stacking speed: under 1 s per sheet for Z-folding and single-sheet stacking","Stacking accuracy: under 200–300 µm","Mechanical separator preload","Z-folding: sheets placed laterally into the folded separator web"],
  alts:["Single-sheet stacking","Lamination — electrode sheets laminated with the separator","Pocket stacking — cathode placed in a separator pocket, then stacked with the anode"],
  innov:["Growth of stacking speed in sheets per second while stacking accuracy also improves","New stacking technologies to reduce cycle times","Handling of large-format electrode sheets"],
  qInf:["Position detection and alignment of different sheet sizes with a vacuum gripper","Mechanical pre-tensioning of the separator"],
  qFeat:["Positioning accuracy of anode and cathode sheets","Damage-free electrode surfaces and edges","Avoidance of electrostatic charging"],
  sop:["Verify dew point and static control","Load magazines, confirm polarity per side","Calibrate vision to the sheet datum","Set separator pre-tension","Stack and verify layer count","Tape the stack and hand over"] },

{ id:"winding", no:"08", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Winding", machine:"winding", routes:"cyl prism",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"very dry, −30…−60 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 20–30 M (winding)", takt:"up to 30 cells/min (cyl)",
  purpose:"Wind anode, cathode and two separators into a jelly roll — the cylindrical and prismatic route.",
  inp:"Daughter rolls, 4 webs", out:"Jelly roll, taped",
  parts:[
    ["Four webs","FEED","Cathode, anode and two separator webs are drawn off together. The sequence is the same as the stacking order, just continuous."],
    ["Winding mandrel","WIND","A centre pin for cylindrical cells, a flat mandrel for prismatic. The flat mandrel is the only reason a prismatic jelly roll is prismatic."],
    ["Taping","FIX","An adhesive strip secures the final turn so the roll cannot unwind during handling."],
    ["Jelly roll","OUTPUT","Up to 30 cells/min cylindrical, up to 6 cells/min prismatic. Tab welding is often integrated into the winder for cylindrical cells."]],
  params:["Up to 30 cells/min (cylindrical)","Up to 6 cells/min (prismatic)","Tab welding integrated in the cylindrical winder"],
  alts:["Reference route shown; equipment configuration varies by manufacturer"],
  innov:["Increasing machine throughput","Increasing the winding diameter","Functional integration of the centre pin, for example as heat dissipation","Integration of the notching process"],
  qInf:["Winding speed","Web tension","Web edge control","Avoidance of electrostatic charging"],
  qFeat:["Positioning accuracy of anode and cathode foils","Damage-free electrode surfaces and edges"],
  sop:["Thread all four webs and confirm the order","Set individual web tensions","Check edge alignment on the first roll","Confirm tab weld position","Verify roll diameter and tape","Transfer without radial load"] },

{ id:"packPouch", no:"09", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Packaging — pouch", machine:"packPouch", routes:"pouch",
  env:{iso:"min. ISO 7", dew:"very dry, −30…−60 °C", temp:"22 ± 2 °C"}, cost:"€ 20–35 M (packaging, pouch cells)", takt:"—",
  purpose:"Weld the tabs, put the stack into deep-drawn aluminium composite foil and seal three of the four sides.",
  inp:"Taped stack", out:"Pouch cell, one side open",
  parts:[
    ["Deep drawing","FORM","The pouch foil — polyamide / aluminium / polypropylene composite — is drawn up to 10 mm deep to make the cavity. Done in line or bought pre-drawn."],
    ["Tab welding","JOIN","All anode current collectors are welded together and to the negative tab, all cathode collectors to the positive tab. Ultrasonic or laser welding. The guide names the ultrasonic parameter set — frequency, amplitude, pressure, time — without fixing values, because they belong to the joint."],
    ["Insertion","LOAD","The stack is placed into the deep-drawn cavity."],
    ["Partial sealing","SEAL","Three sides are sealed gas-tight by impulse or contact sealing. The rule of thumb on the shop floor: 1 mm of seal seam ≈ one year of cell life. One side is left open for filling."]],
  params:["Deep-drawing of pouch film: up to 10 mm","Parameter set for ultrasonic welding: frequency, amplitude, pressure, time","Sealing temperature and pressure","Aluminium composite film: polyamide / aluminium / polypropylene","Rule of thumb: 1 mm seal-seam width corresponds to roughly one year of calendrical service life"],
  alts:["Book folding — one foil with two drawn cavities, folded like a book and sealed"],
